{"id":"g.math.nonlinear-functions.3.930a0e83a6","section":"math","domain":"advanced","skill":"nonlinear-functions","difficulty":3,"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = x^2 + 5x$. The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = f(x - 4) - 6$. What is the value of $g(-3)$?","answer":["8"],"explanation":"$g(-3) = f(-3 - 4) - 6 = f(-7) - 6$. Since $f(-7) = 14$, $g(-3) = 8$."},
{"id":"g.math.nonlinear-functions.3.e1edc3aa78","section":"math","domain":"advanced","skill":"nonlinear-functions","difficulty":3,"prompt":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = -x^2 - x - 2$. The function $g$ is defined by $g(x) = f(x - 5) + 5$. What is the value of $g(1)$?","answer":["-9"],"explanation":"$g(1) = f(1 - 5) + 5 = f(-4) + 5$. Since $f(-4) = -14$, $g(1) = -9$."}
